  "memories": [
    "A .kuhul program is a JSON file with a top-level 'folds' array. Each fold is an object with 'type':'fold', 'name' (Pop/Wo/Yax/Sek/Ch'en/Xul), and 'nodes' array.",
    "Folds execute in order: Pop receives input, Wo constructs semantic state, Yax resolves micronauts and capabilities, Sek executes invocations (invoke MEM-u, invoke REASON-u, etc.), Ch'en evaluates results, Xul collapses surviving state.",
    "A .kprog program is an XJSON file using @verbs: @seq (sequential), @par (parallel), @if (conditional), @coverage (read ExecState), @log (emit message), @var/@set (state variable). Executed by XCFERuntime's DispatchVerb method.",
    "Program nodes come in 7 types: literal (constant), assign (target + value), ref (state lookup), call (function + args), if (conditional), block (group), emit (output).",
    "SemanticMemory.kuhul defines a micronaut mixture: MEM-u(0.40), REASON-u(0.20), VERIFY-u(0.20), PLAN-u(0.10), NET-u(0.10). These weights determine execution priority in Sek invocations.",
    "The Program Engine (Invoke-KuhulProgram) loads a .kuhul file, walks its fold structure, processes each node type, dispatches call nodes to handlers, and returns contributions and state at Xul collapse.",
    "BOSS.kuhul sets coverage_threshold=0.7 and runs discover->curate->verify->promote. BOSS.kprog reads ExecState coverage and decides REFOLD vs COLLAPSE."
  ],
